  "text": "1\nCommunity\nClassroom\nCalendar\nMembers\nMap\nLeaderboards\nAbout\nChase AI Community\n1\n7\nChase Hannegan\n👑\nJul '25 • 🧠Lessons\nSocial Media Poster (9 Platforms)\nMaking content can be fun, but manually posting it to every single social media platform out there sure isn't. This automation solves that problem.\nIn this tutorial, I'll show you how to build a powerful n8n automation that lets you post to 9 social media platforms at once using the Blotato API. Highly modular, this workflow can easily be integrated into any AI system you currently use that requires any form of social media posting, saving you tons of time.\nIf you decide to use my mock data from m... See more\n14:05\nBlotato_Social_Media_Poster_Template (1).json\nFile • 14kb\nLike\n16\n7 comments\n3\nNoe Meza\n• Jul '25\nHey Chase, I'm getting a node error for instagram that I have not been able to troubleshoot. I've asked chatgpt to analyze the JSON syntax and and provided me with a format which I copied and pasted here. Yet still have the same error. Any insights where to find a fix? {\n\"post\": {\n\"target\": {\n\"targetType\": \"instagram\"\n},\n\"content\": {\n\"text\": \"{{ $('Get Content From Google Sheets').item.json.Caption }}\",\n\"platform\": \"instagram\",\n\"mediaUrls\": [\"{{ $json.url }}\"]\n},\n\"accountId\": \"YOUR-ID-HERE\"\n}\n}\nI got the con... See more\n0\nReply\n7\nChase Hannegan\n👑\n• Jul '25\n@Noe Meza \"accountId\": \"YOUR-ID-HERE\"\nYou need to replace that with your appropriate account id\n1\nReply\n3\nNoe Meza\n• Jul '25\ngot it fixed. thanks\n0\nReply\n2\nJoseph Colley\n• Sep '25\nI need this and I want to learn this!\n0\nReply\n1\nEreena Swan\n• Sep '25\nCan you post the same video on all platforms? I thought that all social media platforms always want their own unique videos? tnx\n0\nReply\n1\nAhmed Karam\n• Feb 20\nvideo url cannot be binary!\nurl is mainly to expose video to internet as to placed on social media but what should i do if i have video on 